Subject: [PATCH] tools: always build host lzop/liblzo

Vendor U-Boot configs enable CONFIG_MULTI_DTB_FIT_LZO=y
(qca/src/u-boot/configs/ipq9574_*_defconfig and
qca/src/u-boot-2025/configs/ipq9574_*_defconfig), so the U-Boot Makefile
builds fit-dtb.blob.lzo by invoking the host `lzop` binary
(qca/src/u-boot/Makefile:1168, qca/src/u-boot-2025/Makefile:1213).

In this tree the host tools liblzo/lzop are only queued when
CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS is set (liblzo) or when CONFIG_SDK /
CONFIG_TARGET_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_LZO is set (lzop).  Our minimal
configuration has none of them, so both u-boot packages fail with:

    /bin/sh: 1: lzop: not found
    make[4]: *** [Makefile:1168: fit-dtb.blob.lzo] Error 127

Enabling CONFIG_TARGET_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_LZO would change the
initramfs image payload (currently COMPRESSION_NONE) and CONFIG_SDK
changes far more of the build.  Build the two host tools unconditionally
instead; this affects only host tools, not target/firmware contents.

Observed on the first G3 build, 2026-10-21.

---
--- a/tools/Makefile
+++ b/tools/Makefile
@@ -70,12 +70,12 @@
 tools-y += xz
 tools-y += zip
 tools-y += zlib
-tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS),y) += liblzo
+tools-y += liblzo
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_B43_TOOLS),y) += b43-tools
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_BZIP2_TOOLS),y) += bzip2
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_ISL),y) += isl
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_LZ4_TOOLS),y) += lz4
-tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_LZO_TOOLS),y) += lzop
+tools-y += lzop
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(BUILD_TOOLCHAIN),y) += gmp mpc mpfr
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(CONFIG_TARGET_apm821xx)$(CONFIG_TARGET_gemini),y) += genext2fs
 tools-$(if $(CONFIG_BUILD_ALL_HOST_TOOLS)$(CONFIG_TARGET_ath79),y) += lzma-old squashfs3-lzma
